  "text_sanskrit": "सर्वस्य चाहं हृदि सन्निविष्टो मत्तः स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनञ्च । वेदैश्च सर्वैरहमेव वेद्यो वेदान्तकृद्वेदविदेव चाहम् ॥ १५-१५ ॥",
  "itrans": "sarvasya chAhaM hR^idi sanniviShTo mattaH smR^itirj~nAnamapohana~ncha . vedaishcha sarvairahameva vedyo vedAntakR^idvedavideva chAham .. 15-15 ..",
  "translation": "And I am seated in the heart of every being; from Me proceed memory, perception and misapprehension; what is by all the Vedas made known is I alone; He who has made known the conclusions of the Vedas is Myself; I alone possess the full knowledge of what the Vedas import.\nV. He who has made known the conclusions of the Vedas: the author of the Brahma Sutra, Vyasa. By all the Vedas: in their primary and comprehensive sense. (15)\nA. The following shows that Sri Krishna is the most exalted (Supreme Being).",
